# book-harness — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env`, adjust, then export before running the CLI / MCP server
# (the project does NOT auto-load .env files):
#
#     set -a; source .env; set +a       # bash/zsh
#     export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)   # alternative one-liner
#     env "$(cat .env)" book-harness-mcp    # per-invocation
#
# Nothing here is strictly REQUIRED — every variable has a working default
# (Ollama on localhost + the built-in model preference lists). Sections
# marked [required-if...] describe when a value must be set.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model serving (CLI `run` / `bakeoff` / `drift`, MCP translate_chunk)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the model server.
#   http://localhost:11434           → Ollama (native /api/generate) [default]
#   http://<host>:<port>/v1          → OpenAI-compatible (vLLM, llama.cpp
#                                      `llama-server`, LM Studio, …): the
#                                      trailing /v1 auto-selects the
#                                      chat-completions wire protocol
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# Wire protocol override: auto | ollama | openai
# `auto` (default) = openai when the host URL ends in /v1, ollama otherwise.
#BOOK_HARNESS_API=auto

# API key for OpenAI-compatible endpoints, sent as `Authorization: Bearer …`.
# [required-if] the server enforces authentication (vLLM --api-key, LM Studio
# tokens, hosted endpoints). Ignored for plain Ollama.
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Seconds per generate call before the client gives up (long technical
# paragraphs on CPU-scale models can take minutes).
BOOK_HARNESS_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=900

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model roles (see README "Model serving → Role assignment via env")
#
# each value is a comma- or space-separated preference list; see the note
# above. CASCADE: unset roles inherit — QE falls back to ASSIST, ASSIST to
# TRANSLATION. The FORMAT role does NOT inherit (it has its own general
# instruct defaults: qwen3.8, gemma4, k2-horizon, then qwen2.5:14b /
# llama3.1:8b) so a dedicated MT model is never reused for layout work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Translation role: chunk MT, drift/compliance re-translation, bake-off
# candidates, MCP `translate_chunk`.
BOOK_HARNESS_TRANSLATION_MODELS=hy-mt2-30b-a3b,hy-mt2-7b,qwen2.5:14b,llama3.1:8b

# Assist role (instruct jobs): refinement (MQM estimate / A/B verify),
# rolling chapter summaries. Default: same list as TRANSLATION_MODELS.
#BOOK_HARNESS_ASSIST_MODELS=

# QE role: LLM quality-estimation judge, bake-off judge (--judge overrides).
# Default: same list as ASSIST_MODELS.
#BOOK_HARNESS_QE_MODELS=

# Format role (M5): per-page AI formatting pass — layout-only rewrite,
# general instruct models (NOT the MT model).
#BOOK_HARNESS_FORMAT_MODELS=qwen3.8,gemma4,k2-horizon,qwen2.5:14b,llama3.1:8b

# Singular aliases are also accepted (single-element list):
#BOOK_HARNESS_TRANSLATION_MODEL=
#BOOK_HARNESS_ASSIST_MODEL=
#BOOK_HARNESS_QE_MODEL=
#BOOK_HARNESS_FORMAT_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts (MCP server reads these; the CLI takes --run-root/--model
# flags which win over these for its commands)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Runs root: where runs/<book-id>/ live-artifact directories are created.
BOOK_HARNESS_RUNS=runs

# Cache directory for the arabterm SQLite download (gunzipped once).
# [required-if] the default ~/.cache is not writable (containers, CI).
BOOK_HARNESS_CACHE=~/.cache/book-harness

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional extras (only matter when their pip extra is installed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# gliner extra (zero-shot term extraction): HF access is needed on first
# download of urchade/gliner_multi-v2.1. Without a token the pipeline falls
# back to n-gram-only mining.
#HF_TOKEN=

# qe extra (cometkiwi reference-free QE): downloads Unbabel/wmt22-cometkiwi-da
# on first use; CC-BY-NC — personal use only.
#HF_TOKEN= (same variable as above)
